<!-- ============ PROBLEM + REAL PROBLEM — combined ============ -->
<section id="problem" class="real bg-grid bg-grid-dark">
  <div class="wrap real-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-label">The problem</div>
      <h2>Your advice is not the bottleneck. Mortgage admin is.</h2>
      <p>You already know how to advise. What slows you down is everything around it: checking statements, matching payslips, spotting credit issues, proving deposit source, writing notes, evidencing protection, and chasing missing documents.</p>
      <p>Every hour spent on that is an hour not advising, or being home, and even when it is done, the case still comes back from the lender, from compliance, or from the client.</p>
      <div class="problem-cards">
        <div class="pcard">
          <span class="pcard-k">01 / Doc review</span>
          <h4>Bank statements</h4>
          <p>Income, conduct, gambling, transfers, debts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard pcard-dark">
          <span class="pcard-k">02 / Adverse</span>
          <h4>Credit files</h4>
          <p>Missed payments, CCJs, debts, hard searches.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard">
          <span class="pcard-k">03 / Evidence</span>
          <h4>Case notes</h4>
          <p>Income, deposit, suitability, rationale.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pcard pcard-lime">
          <span class="pcard-k">04 / Client work</span>
          <h4>Client chase</h4>
          <p>Draft WhatsApps, emails, and follow-up questions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="real-col">
      <div class="transcript reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="sec-label">The real problem</div>
        <h2 style="margin-top: 12px; margin-bottom: 28px;">The admin around each case sets the cap.</h2>

        <blockquote>
          I feel like I'm working at <span class="hl">full capacity</span>, but I can't grow because admin eats my time.
        </blockquote>
        <div class="sig">— Advisor using AI Mortgage Admin</div>

        <div class="body-txt">
          <strong>More cases means more statements to check</strong>, more credit files to read, more clients to chase, more notes to tidy. So the advisor either stops taking more cases, or takes them and pays for it with evenings and weekends.
          <br><br>
          AI Mortgage Admin is built to <span class="lime">lift that cap.</span> Not by changing how you advise. By taking the admin work that sits between advice given and case submitted off your desk.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ FIXES — ledger ============ -->
<section class="fixes">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-label reveal">Why the usual fixes do not work</div>
    <h2 class="reveal reveal-delay-1">Hiring a case manager takes months. Templates do not read the file. Generic AI does not know a CCJ from a hard search.</h2>

    <div class="ledger">
      <div class="ledger-row fail reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="n">01 / TRIED</div>
        <div>
          <h4>A case manager</h4>
        </div>
        <p>Costs a full salary before it helps. Needs training on your firm's process, your network's quirks, and your protection rationale. Still leaves the advisor doing the judgement calls.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row fail reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <div class="n">02 / TRIED</div>
        <div>
          <h4>WhatsApp and email templates</h4>
        </div>
        <p>Generic "please send more documents" messages. They do not look at the file, do not know what is actually missing, and the client ignores them or sends the wrong thing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row fail reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <div class="n">03 / TRIED</div>
        <div>
          <h4>Generic AI chatbots</h4>
        </div>
        <p>Wait for you to explain the whole case from scratch every time. They do not understand gifted deposits, overseas transfers, defaults versus CCJs, or why a declined cover needs a file note.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row win reveal reveal-delay-5">
        <div class="n">04 / HOW IT FITS</div>
        <div>
          <h4>A review and drafting layer. You stay the advisor on the file.</h4>
        </div>
        <p>Every flag, every WhatsApp, every email is <strong>reviewed by you before anything moves.</strong> It does not submit, send, or sign anything off. Built for mortgage and protection files specifically, not generic document review. Your compliance wording, your network's process, and your approved tone are configured at setup.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ HOW — staircase ============ -->
<section id="how" class="how bg-grid">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-label reveal">How it works</div>
    <h2 class="reveal reveal-delay-1">Four steps from messy file to submission-ready.</h2>

    <div class="staircase">
      <div class="stair stair-1 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <span class="step-n">01</span>
        <h3>Upload the case documents</h3>
        <p>Bank statements, credit file, payslips, deposit evidence, protection notes, fact find.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stair stair-2 reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <span class="step-n">02</span>
        <h3>AI Mortgage Admin reviews the file</h3>
        <p>Checks every document, cross-references the story, flags what is missing or risky.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stair stair-3 reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <span class="step-n">03</span>
        <h3>You get flags, questions, and draft messages</h3>
        <p>Review the gaps, approve the WhatsApp or email chase, decide what goes to the client.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stair stair-4 reveal reveal-delay-5">
        <span class="step-n">04</span>
        <h3>You submit a cleaner case</h3>
        <p>File goes to the lender with fewer gaps, fewer weak notes, and fewer avoidable queries.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CASE ============ -->
<section id="case" class="case">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-label">[ Case study ]</div>

    <div class="case-layout">
      <div class="case-left reveal">
        <div class="case-pdf">
          <span class="pk">Case study · 01</span>
          <h4>The file looked ready. The review found three things before the lender did.</h4>
          <div class="pdf-sub">First-time buyer purchase. £30,000 deposit. A closer look before submission.</div>

          <div class="case-outcome">
            <div class="item">
              <span class="k">Outcome</span>
              <span class="v">Corrected before submission</span>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
              <span class="k">Lender queries avoided</span>
              <span class="v">2 foreseeable</span>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
              <span class="k">Offer issued</span>
              <span class="v">4 days later</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pdf-pages">
            <b>AI Mortgage Admin</b>
            <span>12 pages</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a class="btn btn-on-dark case-cta" href="#book">Download the full case study <span class="arrow">↓</span></a>
      </div>

      <div class="case-copy reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <svg class="pdf-hint-arrow" width="140" height="49" viewBox="0 0 380 132" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M1.44574 61.1935C5.23881 71.6566 16.7955 64.7185 23.614 61.6428C35.3007 55.9435 47.9577 52.9106 60.3997 49.3619C83.9192 41.9887 108.212 37.8563 132.641 34.9294C157.522 30.0079 183.236 33.026 207.182 40.9376C183.77 53.9122 153.66 81.0519 168.379 110.216C175.948 124.291 192.779 134.463 208.911 131.256C238.839 125.568 279.667 74.6545 252.929 47.6279C299.216 49.7015 323.858 72.3163 357.971 99.9322C361.278 102.457 364.175 105.586 367.697 107.775C375.232 111.833 383.187 102.199 377.767 95.5513C353.57 75.8968 329.896 53.8897 301.066 41.1857C278.681 33.6456 253.731 29.0003 230.167 32.1792C207.385 22.6752 182.827 16.4308 158.039 16.3897C127.824 17.7823 97.5398 22.9522 68.199 30.3273C47.5646 35.954 26.9417 41.5376 7.64304 50.9397C3.00375 51.7153 0.107731 56.7864 1.44574 61.1935ZM182.568 86.0698C191.622 68.2207 209.814 55.957 228.223 49.2408C235.559 53.5751 246.271 59.6258 245.686 69.366C245.706 69.2363 245.728 69.1063 245.749 68.9765C245.756 68.764 245.762 68.5513 245.769 68.339C241.838 89.9531 224.799 112.882 201.929 115.758C188.306 114.388 175.531 99.5471 182.568 86.0698Z"/>
          <path d="M0.00134323 66.0661C-0.121404 74.1831 8.46788 76.029 14.9021 76.7328C28.114 79.009 41.2882 81.4408 54.3712 84.3637C60.9683 85.1908 67.0892 88.9615 73.6263 89.1714C80.5725 88.2328 82.7969 78.5809 77.0331 74.6251C58.152 66.6058 36.9941 64.781 16.9606 60.7204C21.7513 43.5116 32.5459 28.4019 41.1777 12.9929C42.4149 11.082 43.1307 9.02166 42.7477 6.72538C41.9198 -0.0972456 31.9611 -2.58451 28.2025 3.31897C23.6449 10.6168 19.3715 18.0967 15.1861 25.6116C8.33517 38.1859 0.332096 51.3684 0.00134323 66.0661Z"/>
        </svg>

        <h2>The file looked ready. The review found <em>three things</em> before the lender did.</h2>

        <div class="cs-cards-stack">
          <div class="case-card cc-neutral">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <span class="cc-icon">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
              </span>
              <h3>The situation</h3>
            </div>
            <p>A residential purchase case for a first-time buyer on a joint application. Income evidence, three months of bank statements, a £30,000 deposit, and protection recommendation notes were all on file. The advisor was ready to submit.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-card cc-alert">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <span class="cc-icon">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0Z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
              </span>
              <h3>What AI Mortgage Admin caught</h3>
            </div>
            <p>A £8,500 family transfer with no gifted deposit letter. An overtime income note that did not match the salary credits on two months of statements. A weak protection rationale where critical illness cover had been declined on budget grounds without evidence. It then drafted the client WhatsApp and the email to the compliance checker.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-card cc-success">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <span class="cc-icon">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
              </span>
              <h3>The outcome</h3>
            </div>
            <p>The advisor corrected the file before submission. Two foreseeable lender queries avoided. Compliance signed off first time. Client returned the gifted deposit letter and overtime explanation the same evening. Offer issued four days later.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ COMPARE ============ -->
<section class="cmp bg-dots">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cmp-top reveal">
      <div class="cmp-head">
        <div class="sec-label">Compared to</div>
        <h2>What most advisors try before this, and why the gap is still there.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp-foot">
        The point is not that any of these are wrong. The point is that each one solves part of the problem. AI Mortgage Admin was built to cover the part that keeps falling back on the advisor.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="compare-wrap">
      <table class="compare-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>
              <span class="cmp-q">Can it <em>actually</em> do the work properly?</span>
            </th>
            <th>
              <div class="cmp-col">
                <span class="cmp-ic">
                  <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/></svg>
                </span>
                <span class="cmp-lbl">Case manager</span>
              </div>
            </th>
            <th>
              <div class="cmp-col">
                <span class="cmp-ic">
                  <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="8" y1="13" x2="16" y2="13"/><line x1="8" y1="17" x2="16" y2="17"/></svg>
                </span>
                <span class="cmp-lbl">Templates</span>
              </div>
            </th>
            <th>
